{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791634987,"nonce":"AXqslZ9a4S/qB3IZ2X5xYM+OBLM=","message":"Reported in cn_demo's navigation bar: \"Home\" folds onto two lines (\"Hom\" / \"e\"), and the chevrons after \"Products\" and \"Services\" sit further from their labels than the spacing says.\n\n\n`FontTextMeasurer::measure_with_options` and `line_spans` looked a face up with `get_for_render_with_style`, which reads only the cache (\"never load during measurement\"). `preload_generic_fonts` loads weight 400 of each generic. So the first layout of any medium, semibold or bold text found no face and fell back to `EstimatedTextMeasurer` (0.55 x font size per character), while the renderer's `resolve_font_with_style` loaded the face and drew real glyphs. Layout never ran again for it.\n\nMeasured with real fonts (cn_demo's theme bundle, 14px medium, offscreen):\n\n| label | layout box (estimate) | drawn |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Home | 31.0 | 36.5 |\n| Products | 61.0 | 54.1 |\n| Services | 62.0 | 52.0 |\n\n\"Home\"'s box is narrower than the text, so it wraps; \"Products\" and \"Services\" get boxes wider than their text, which is the extra gap before the chevron.\n\nSeparately, `Text::weight` (and `medium()`, `bold()`, ...) and `italic()` did not re-measure, unlike `size()` and `font_family()`, so `measured_width` kept the regular weight's width. The paint path compares it with the box to decide wrapping: at 14px, \"Products and services\" in light reported 128.8 against 126.6 drawn.\n\n\n- `FontRegistry::resolve_styled` holds the renderer's resolution order (cached, then the named family in the style, then the generic in the style, then the normal style, then sans-serif). The renderer and both measurer paths call it, so text is measured in the face it is drawn in, loading the face the first time.\n- `weight()` and `italic()` measure again.\n- The navigation bar's labels are `no_wrap`, as shadcn's `w-max` trigger is (separate commit with the nav refactor).\n\n\n`blinc_layout/tests/fallback_measure.rs` (text_measurer feature): `a_weight_not_yet_loaded_measures_as_it_draws` measures before drawing, as layout does, at 500/600/700 (\"Home\" at 500 measured 30.8 against 36.5 drawn before the fix); `a_label_reports_its_width_in_its_own_weight` for light and bold (fails without the weight re-measure).\n\n\nThe loads happen lazily, the first time text in a style is measured, which is the same load the renderer does when it first draws that text in the same frame. Nothing is preloaded, so an app with a renderer does no scan it did not already do; the load moves from paint to layout. A host measuring without a renderer now loads real faces instead of estimating.","files":null}]}